', 'function', 'double', 'Python uses indentation, not brackets, to show which lines belong inside a block. A colon-ended line always needs its body indented one level in, consistently.', 'After any line ending in `:`, check the next line is indented - your editor''s auto-indent usually does this for you, which is exactly why it''s easy to miss when it doesn''t.', NULL, 'published', '0efa631340af77346e55b17c28866bae25c440e3020bbbe6fc7154489d2fd71e', NOW());
